                <pb facs="0368" n="334" sameAs="frus:frus1897/pg334"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Olney to Mr. Lazo Arriaga.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1897-01-27"><hi rendition="#italic">January 27,
                        1897</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 25.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge the receipt
                    of your note of the 15th instant, and to inform you in reply that Mr. D. Lynch
                    Pringle, consul-general of the United States at Guatemala City, has been
                    appointed honorary commissioner of this Government at the Central American
                    Exposition, to be opened on March 15 next.</p>
                <p>Accept, sir, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Richard Olney.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
